sources:
    - id: smith1962
      title: An Experimental Study of Competitive Market Behavior
      authors: Vernon L. Smith
      year: 1962
      finding: Strong tendencies toward the competitive equilibrium 'as long as one is able to prohibit collusion and to maintain absolute publicity of all bids, offers, and transactions'.
    - id: plottsmith78
      title: An Experimental Examination of Two Exchange Institutions
      authors: Charles R. Plott and Vernon L. Smith
      year: 1978
      finding: Holding supply and demand fixed, posted-offer pricing converged more slowly than the oral double auction, with prices typically approaching from above.
    - id: coursey
      title: Vernon Smith (Econlib feature)
      authors: Don Coursey
      year: 2002
      finding: As few as four sellers and four buyers produce the competitive outcome in double auctions.

    ```brython sim x 200 y 420 width 510 show code controls ["n","rules"] control_size 16 pane controls hidden true
    import random
    n = Slider(2, 12, default=4, label="Traders per side")
    rules = ["double auction", "posted prices"]
    random.seed(3)
    k = n - n // 4; d = 1.2 / k                  # values and costs cross at $2
    v = [2 + d * (k - j - 0.5) for j in range(n)]
    c = [2 - d * (k - j - 0.5) for j in range(n)]
    wb = [x * random.uniform(0.2, 0.8) for x in v]             # opening bids
    ws = [x + (4 - x) * random.uniform(0.2, 0.8) for x in c]   # opening asks
    price = []
    for t in range(5):
        b, s, nb, ns, pb, ps, row = wb[:], ws[:], list(range(n)), list(range(n)), [0]*n, [0]*n, []
        for step in range(30 * n):
            if not nb or not ns: break
            i, j = random.choice(nb), min(ns, key=lambda j: s[j])
            if rules == "posted prices":
                if s[j] <= v[i]: row.append(s[j]); ps[j] = s[j]; ns.remove(j)
                nb.remove(i); continue
            if random.random() < 0.5: b[i] += random.uniform(0, 0.5) * (v[i] - b[i])
            else: j = random.choice(ns); s[j] -= random.uniform(0, 0.5) * (s[j] - c[j])
            i, j = max(nb, key=lambda i: b[i]), min(ns, key=lambda j: s[j])
            if b[i] >= s[j]:
                row.append((b[i] + s[j]) / 2); pb[i] = ps[j] = row[-1]; nb.remove(i); ns.remove(j)
        wb = [0.9 * pb[i] if pb[i] else (wb[i] + v[i]) / 2 for i in range(n)]
        ws = [1.1 * ps[j] if ps[j] else (ws[j] + c[j]) / 2 for j in range(n)]
        slot = [None] * 12
        for q, p in enumerate(row): slot[int((q + 0.5) * 12 / len(row))] = round(p, 2)
        price += slot
    eq = [2] + [None] * 58 + [2]
    ```
    text rd "{sim.n} buyers, {sim.n} sellers" x 270 y 590 font_size 32 hidden true
    text rr "{sim.rules}" #2f6b8f x 270 y 535 font_size 32 hidden true
